// bits/value_stream — the always-available half of the madc value
// stream inserter. madc::value is an INHERENT madc-mode type (owner
// law 2026-08-19: it requires no #include), so streaming one must not
// depend on <ns_madc> or on include order. The declaration still
// cannot precede std::ostream's, so the lexer injects this fragment
// ONCE, at the completion of whichever include first defines the
// ostream guard (_GLIBCXX_OSTREAM / _LIBCPP_OSTREAM — <iostream>,
// <fstream>, <sstream>, or the bare-cout auto-include), madc dialect
// only. Strict C/C++ modes never see it; <ns_madc>'s guarded twin is
// their opt-in — a DECLARATION beside this one is safe (the overload
// registry dedups same-spelling redeclarations), so the twin declares
// only when this fragment declares (the same flavor predicate below)
// and steps aside when this fragment defines the body.
//
// Stream a value EXACTLY as the contained type would stream (owner
// ruling 2026-08-19): each kind forwards to the real inserter, so
// std::hex / setprecision / boolalpha apply the way they do to a plain
// int / double / bool; null streams nothing; array/object/instance are
// not streamable (a stderr notice, nothing written).
//
// TWO RENDERINGS, one publics list (dialect-lean.md's guard model). When
// the script's stdlib flavor is the host's, the declaration resolves
// mangled-direct to the real madc::operator<< (src/madc_value.cpp). When
// it is not — linux -stdlib=libc++ on a libstdc++-built madc, the parity
// lane; __MADC_HOST_LIBCPP__ is the lexer's build fact, _LIBCPP_VERSION
// the script's — the stream object is the SCRIPT flavor's basic_ostream
// and no host symbol can take it (a std::string marshals by its bytes,
// task #69; a stream cannot), so the inserter is rendered HERE in the
// script's flavor: kind by kind through the carrier's own predicates and
// accessors, the same forwarding the host body does, compiled against the
// stream it is handed. The container-kind notice is the host's one text.
namespace madc {
#if (defined(_LIBCPP_VERSION) && defined(__MADC_HOST_LIBCPP__)) \
 || (!defined(_LIBCPP_VERSION) && !defined(__MADC_HOST_LIBCPP__))
    std::ostream &operator<<(std::ostream &os, const value &v);
#else
    void value_not_streamable_notice(const value &v);
    inline std::ostream &operator<<(std::ostream &os, const value &v)
    {
	if ( v.is_null() )
	    return os;
	if ( v.is_boolean() )
	    return os << v.as_boolean();
	if ( v.is_integer() )
	    return os << v.as_integer();
	if ( v.is_real() )
	    return os << v.as_real();
	if ( v.is_string() || v.is_bytes() )
	    return os.write(v.data(), v.size());
	value_not_streamable_notice(v);
	return os;
    }
#endif
}
